# leveled-from: dlr/Puppet_Stayman_2N.dlr sha256:859f526adb18945ac6ed3cc779fdc568248d7a826c92a9a105820ce4f76af914
# alias: PuppetStayman2N
# button-text: 2N Puppet
# scenario-title: --- Puppet Stayman after 2NT (20-21)
# gib-works: false
# bba-works: true
# auction-filter: Auction.....\n2N Pass 3C
# convention-card-ns: 21GF-MSTandMSS
# convention-card-ew: 21GF-GIB

/*@chat
--- Puppet Stayman after 2NT (20-21)
After a 2NT opening (20-21 HCP balanced), responder uses 3!C to ask
about opener's major suits.

Opener's responses:
• 3!D - No 5-card major, but has at least one 4-card major
• 3!H - 5-card heart suit
• 3!S - 5-card spade suit
• 3NT - No 4-card or 5-card major

Responder's follow-ups after 3!D (one or both 4-card majors):
• Bid the major you DO NOT hold (with one 4-card major)
  This lets the strong hand (opener) declare if a fit exists.
• 4!D - both 4-card majors, no slam interest; opener picks
• 4!C - both 4-card majors WITH slam interest

After 3!H or 3!S (opener shows 5-card major):
• 3NT - denies a fit
• Bid the OTHER major - slam try agreeing opener's suit
• Raise to game/slam - standard

After 3NT (no majors): natural minor-suit slam investigation.

Bid Puppet 3!C with:
• Any 4-card major (looking for 4-4 fit)
• 3-card support for one or both majors (looking for 5-3 fit)
• Game or slam-going values opposite 20-21 NT

Reference: https://www.bridgebum.com/puppet_stayman.php
@chat*/

dealer south

# South opens 2NT (20-21 balanced)
ntShape = shape(south,any 4333+any 4432+any 5332-5xxx-x5xx)
ntRange = hcp(south)>19 and hcp(south)<22
twoN = ntShape and ntRange

# North's hand qualifies for Puppet:
# - at least one 4-card major, OR
# - 3-card support for both majors (looking for 5-3 fit with opener)
sN = spades(north)
hN = hearts(north)
nHas4SAndNot4H = sN==4 and hN<4
nHas4HAndNot4S = hN==4 and sN<4
nHasBoth4M    = sN==4 and hN==4
nHas3S3H      = sN==3 and hN==3
nQualifies    = nHas4SAndNot4H or nHas4HAndNot4S or nHasBoth4M or nHas3S3H

# Exclude very long suits (would use a different system)
nNoLongSuit = sN<5 and hN<5 and diamonds(north)<6 and clubs(north)<6

# Define HCP zones for North (responder).
# After 2NT (20-21), responder with 5+ HCP can invoke Puppet for game.
# 0-4: too weak (would pass 2NT)
# 5-10: game-going
# 11-13: slam invite
# 14+: slam force
tooWeak    = hcp(north)<5
game       = hcp(north)>4  and hcp(north)<11
slamInvite = hcp(north)>10 and hcp(north)<14
slamForce  = hcp(north)>13

# Leveling: balance game and slam outcomes.
# Game-zone (5-10) is the most common range; slam ranges rarer.
HandType_Game = game
HandType_SlamInv = slamInvite
HandType_SlamForce = slamForce

### BEGIN GENERATED LEVELING ###
# Generated by dealer --write-leveled. Do not edit; edit the stock
# scenario and regenerate, or the two will disagree without saying so.
#
# measured over  80037 deals, seed 1
#
# type         natural    target     keep      seen
# Game         0.84275   0.33333   0.0297     67451
# SlamInv      0.13226   0.33333   0.1889     10586
# SlamForce    0.02499   0.33333   1.0000      2000
#
# exactness      1.000  (full)
# acceptance     0.0750 of qualifying deals
# cost           about 9147 deals dealt per deal kept
# precision      keeps set by SlamForce, the rarest, seen 2000 times (+-2.2%); expect the mix within +-0.74 points

roll = (rnd(1000) % 1000 + 1000) % 1000

level_Game = HandType_Game and roll < 30
level_SlamInv = HandType_SlamInv and roll < 189
level_SlamForce = HandType_SlamForce
levelTheDeal = level_Game or level_SlamInv or level_SlamForce
### END GENERATED LEVELING ###

# Combine
twoN and nQualifies and nNoLongSuit
and (HandType_Game or HandType_SlamInv or HandType_SlamForce) and levelTheDeal

action printoneline,
average "Has 4!S only       " 100 * nHas4SAndNot4H,
average "Has 4!H only       " 100 * nHas4HAndNot4S,
average "Has both 4M        " 100 * nHasBoth4M,
average "Has 3-3 in majors  " 100 * nHas3S3H,
average "Game range (5-10)  " 100 * game,
average "Slam invite (11-13)" 100 * slamInvite,
average "Slam force (14+)   " 100 * slamForce,
